  "step_3": "First, the information relevant to the decision reason (variance) is available from the lotteries and can be computed. Second, the individual did not consider variance or any related concept such as risk, dispersion, or stability of outcomes. Instead, their justification was based on expected value and the magnitude of the winning probability. The decision reason’s rule (preferring lower variance) would lead to choosing Lottery A, but the individual chose Lottery B based on higher expected value and high probability—reasons that are inconsistent with the variance-based rule. Therefore, the individual did not use the variance-based decision reason. The assessment is certain that the reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
