  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on comparing the variance of the lotteries and preferring the one with lower variance. The individual did not mention variance, risk, or any measure of dispersion. Instead, their justification was based on the probability of winning any amount (i.e., non-zero outcome), which is a different criterion (maximizing the chance of a non-zero payoff). Although the decision reason would lead to the same choice (A) because A has lower variance, the individual’s reasoning process did not involve variance at all. The information considered (expected value, probability of non-zero outcome) does not include variance, and the justification is based on a different principle (maximizing chance of any gain). Therefore, the individual did not use the variance-based reason to make the decision. The final assessment is not based on whether the outcome matches, but on whether the reasoning process aligns with the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
